003.xhtml#c2-the-danger-of-an-untouchable-national-champion"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-39" playOrder="39"><navLabel><text>Reporting and sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-reporting-and-sources"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-40" playOrder="40"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-41" playOrder="41"><navLabel><text>Nvidia’s board faces the Huang problem</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#chapter-3"/><navPoint id="nav-42" playOrder="42"><navLabel><text>The phone, the security workers and the NDA</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-the-phone-the-security-workers-and-the-nda"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-43" playOrder="43"><navLabel><text>The founder is covered by the code</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-the-founder-is-covered-by-the-code"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-44" playOrder="44"><navLabel><text>Directors have the power to remove the CEO</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-directors-have-the-power-to-remove-the-ceo"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-45" playOrder="45"><navLabel><text>The lawsuit puts public assurances before a judge</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-the-lawsuit-puts-public-assurances-before-a-judge"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-46" playOrder="46"><navLabel><text>AI finance depends on the next decisions</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-ai-finance-depends-on-the-next-decisions"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-47" playOrder="47"><navLabel><text>Corporate obligations extend beyond the CEO</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-corporate-obligations-extend-beyond-the-ceo"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-48" playOrder="48"><navLabel><text>Washington may seek greater influence</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-washington-may-seek-greater-influence"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-49" playOrder="49"><navLabel><text>Restoring control over decisions</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-restoring-control-over-decisions"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-50" playOrder="50"><navLabel><text>Reporting and sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-reporting-and-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-51" playOrder="51"><navLabel><text>Nvidia after Huang: Washington faces questions</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#chapter-4"/><navPoint id="nav-52" playOrder="52"><navLabel><text>Singapore puts requests for evidence on the record</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-singapore-puts-requests-for-evidence-on-the-record"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-53" playOrder="53"><navLabel><text>Congress asks Washington to preserve its decisions</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-congress-asks-washington-to-preserve-its-decisions"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-54" playOrder="54"><navLabel><text>The new leadership inherits the financing chain</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-the-new-leadership-inherits-the-financing-chain"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-55" playOrder="55"><navLabel><text>Revenue promises need financing before delivery</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-revenue-promises-need-financing-before-delivery"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-56" playOrder="56"><navLabel><text>Three routes to a permanent chief executive</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-three-routes-to-a-permanent-chief-executive"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-57" playOrder="57"><navLabel><text>Washington has an interest in the next negotiation</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-washington-has-an-interest-in-the-next-negotiation"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-58" playOrder="58"><navLabel><text>The next test is the documentary record</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-the-next-test-is-the-documentary-record"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-59" playOrder="59"><navLabel><text>Reporting